ith the process that started it, even when that process is killed,\n      on every backend, as bubblewrap's `--die-with-parent` already gives.\n    steps_to_reproduce:\n      - \"Write a script that calls `runProcess` with `node -e \\\"setInterval(()=>{},1000)\\\"` and a 60 s timeout, then kills itself with SIGKILL after 300 ms.\"\n      - \"Run it with `node`: once it is killed, `ps -Ao pid,ppid,command` shows the `node -e setInterval` process with parent 1, running until it is stopped by its pid.\"\n    root_cause: >\n      The group is detached so that a timeout can end it as a whole, and only the runner's own timer or abort signal\n      ends it; nothing ties the group's life to the runner's, outside bubblewrap.\n    evidence: >\n      Reproduced on 2026-10-12 on macOS with the script above (not committed): the command, pid 85454, ran with parent 1\n      after its caller was killed, and was stopped by its pid. Run alone to its end, test/v1-adapters/sandbox.test.ts\n      leaves no process behind. The defect predates the branch e40s03, which neither introduces nor changes\n      `runProcess`.\n    risk_level: medium\n    follow_ups: >\n      Tie the process group to the runner on every backend, for instance behind a parent that ends the group once its\n      input from the runner closes, and hold it with a test that kills the runner and finds the command gone.\n    status: open\n583:      Probe on 2026-10-01 against the head of the branch: the call above throws, and the runner's catch\n971:      Read on the branch: the node:test witness source in `nodeTestWitnesses` and the `text.includes(JSON.stringify(name))`\n2064:      Read at the self-review of `e11s07` on its branch: `node-structure.ts` returns on `short_of` before calling\n2523:      Reported by the review of e38s07 (round 1) and read on the branch: `contestationConclude` reads `examiner_id` only\n3497:      15, `v2-kernel` 395. Not introduced by a branch: the suite was never run confined before.\n3726 sp